  "requested_entire_literal_mathematical_scope": "Read all11 full public proofs/6definitions/one abbrev/3private analytic enclosures, full used actual primary proofs, both complete selected coordinate/form sources and the exact entire131 with preceding weighted-inner-product context. Decide the entire unit independently only after actual Euclidean pairing/norms/angle identity,81.9-degree approximation, actual PD diagonal metric/coordinate2 doubling, weighted pairing/norms/obtuse angle and metric-dependent lengths/perpendicularity are assessed. No parent or neighboring unit is included.",
  "exact_fixture_assessment": "Actual x=(1,2),y=(3,-1) are EuclideanSpace vectors. Their actual pairing1/normssqrt5,sqrt10 give actual Mathlib angle arccos(1/sqrt50). The degree result is strict absolute error<.05 from81.9, using rational sine Taylor remainders and rigorous pi bounds, not a floating evaluation.",
  "genuine_angle_enclosure_route": "Exact inverse sqrt50 lies(.14142,.14143); actual sine(.1418) lies below and sine(.142) above it. Genuine inverse-sine monotonicity on[-1,1] gives arcsin in(.1418,.142); arccos=pi/2-arcsin and3.1415<pi<3.1416 give strict81.85<angledeg<81.95.",
  "weighted_metric_assessment": "The actual diagonalM=diag(1,4) is PD. Its all-input pairing is exactly the Euclidean pairing after(x1,x2)->(x1,2x2), so this is a true weighted metric realization. The printed weighted pair has pairing-5, norms sqrt17,sqrt13 and actual angle arccos(-5/sqrt221) strictly betweenpi/2 andpi. An actual extra vector(-2,1) is Euclidean-perpendicular to x but has weighted pairing6, and x becomes strictly longer.",
